---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import ClubBase from '../layouts/ClubBase.astro';
import heroPhoto from '../assets/club-evening-run.jpg';
import joinPhoto from '../assets/club-group-photo.jpg';
import { CLUB_CTA } from '@src/shared/club-nav';
import {
  comingUpOn,
  parseClub,
  parseEvents,
  parseMembership,
  parseNewsletters,
  parsePace,
} from '@src/shared/club-content';
import { formatPriceWords } from '@src/shared/money';
import club from '../content/club.json';
import events from '../content/events.json';
import membership from '../content/membership.json';
import newsletters from '../content/newsletters.json';
import pace from '../content/pace.json';
import race from '../content/race.json';

// `/` — the club's front page.
//
// The order answers a stranger's questions in the order they actually arrive: who are you,
// when do you meet, what happens if I turn up, which group, what is on, and what does joining
// cost. A nervous first-timer is the reader throughout.
//
// ## ⚠️ Nightingale Nightmare links to `/nn/`, and takes its date from `race.json`
//
// **`/nn/` and not `/nn/2026/`.** That address is evergreen — it paints on whichever running
// is current from `entries.current_entry_state('nn')` — so a link to it keeps working when
// 2027 is published, and the entry journey from there is untouched by this change.
//
// **The date is read rather than restated.** `race.json` is where it lives, and a copy here
// would be a second place to change it — with a silent failure, because a card showing last
// year's date looks exactly like one showing this year's.
//
// ## The heading, and the one phrase it may not use
//
// ⚠️ **Not "Welcome to Southville Running Club".** The banner rendered directly above already
// reads *"Welcome to Southville Running Club's new website."*, so a heading one line below
// saying almost the same words is duplication a sighted reader skims past and a screen-reader
// user hears twice in a row. The holding page this replaced carried the same note for the same
// reason, and it is the one heading that collides with the chrome.
//
// It was *"Come and run with friends you haven't met yet"* in the mockup. The sentiment is
// right and the stock phrase was not: *"friends you haven't met yet"* reads as dating-app copy,
// which is a strange first impression for a running club. Cutting the clause leaves the
// invitation, which is what the line is for — and the lede beneath already does the
// inclusivity work, so the heading does not need to.
//
// ## What is deliberately not on this page
//
// **No testimonial.** The mockup carries three quotes attributed to "[Member name]". A
// testimonial is a real person saying a real thing with their consent, and the club has not
// supplied one — so the whole section is absent rather than greyed out. It comes back when
// there is a quote to print.
//
// **No club kit card.** Kit is out of scope for this build entirely.
//
// ## The hero photograph
//
// ⚠️ **Two real photographs of identifiable club members, which is a consent question before
// it is a technical one.** About eighty people are recognisable in the hero and about eighteen
// in the membership section.
//
// The rule is that the club supplies photographs **with consent from the people shown**. Both
// were supplied by a club volunteer — the evening-run photograph on **20 September 2026**, the
// group photograph on **21 September 2026** — and consent was confirmed for each. Those
// confirmations are recorded here and in `docs/design/direction-a.md` rather than left in a
// conversation, because a photograph whose consent nobody can evidence has to come down.
//
// ## Which photograph goes where, which was decided rather than defaulted
//
// The group photograph was in the hero for about an hour on 21 September 2026 and moved down.
// Three reasons, and they are worth keeping because the obvious instinct is to lead with the
// biggest picture:
//
//   1. **The hero is selling Tuesday night and that photograph is a race** — numbers, a finish
//      gazebo, a summer field — directly above a facts strip that says *Tuesdays and Thursdays,
//      50p a run*. The evening-run photograph is the thing the page is actually offering.
//   2. ⚠️ **It carries the club's wordmark burnt into it**, so in the hero it sat about 200px
//      below the header's own artwork. WCAG 1.4.5 exempts a logotype, so this was allowed
//      rather than wrong; it simply read as the logo dropped in twice. Beside the membership
//      invitation it reads as a club banner.
//   3. **Eighty faces at hero size are not faces.** Scaled into roughly 580×325px the group
//      becomes a green mass; eighteen people at that size are legible. A nervous first-timer
//      is scanning for *somebody like me*, which a crowd cannot answer and a group can.
//
// It also crops better: the evening-run photograph is exactly 4:3 and the hero slot is 4:3, so
// nothing is lost, where the panoramic group shot lost about 7% of its width up there.
//
// Swapping either is one import and one `alt`; removing one leaves the flat `--club-photo`
// panel the rest of the site still uses.
//
// **`<Image>` rather than `<img>`**, so Astro emits width, height and a modern format at
// build time — the source is 1600×1200 and 382 kB, which is a phone photograph rather than a
// web asset.
//
// ⚠️ **`loading="lazy"` on an image that is above the fold**, which looks wrong and is
// deliberate. This element is `display: none` below 62em — the facts strip has to be inside
// the first screen on a phone, and a photograph above it costs the whole budget. An eager
// image would still be **downloaded** there, so 70% of this club's visitors would pay for a
// picture they never see. A lazy image that is not rendered is not fetched, and a lazy image
// that *is* in the viewport loads immediately, so the desktop case is unaffected.
//
// **The other panels are still flat colour.** `--club-photo`, `aria-hidden`, no text and no
// stripe pattern — see `club.css`. They are replaced by real photographs the same way this
// one was, not filled in.

const { meet, who } = parseClub(club);
const { rows, alsoRunning } = parsePace(pace);
const prices = parseMembership(membership);
const { issues } = parseNewsletters(newsletters);

// **Resolved at build time**, so an expired card leaves the page at the next build rather
// than at midnight. `comingUpOn` compares two UTC instants and never a civil date — the race
// is run the weekend after the clocks change, and that is exactly where a date comparison
// goes wrong by an hour.
const upcoming = comingUpOn(parseEvents(events), new Date());

const latestIssue = issues[0];

/** The date a card shows, read from wherever that fact actually lives. */
function dateFor(source: string): string | null {
  if (source === 'race') return race.date;
  if (source === 'newsletter')
    return latestIssue?.title.replace(/^.*Newsletter /u, '') ?? null;
  return null;
}

// Composed here rather than in the markup, for the reason `ClubFooter` carries at length:
// Prettier reflows adjacent expressions onto separate lines and Astro compresses the newline
// between them to nothing, which silently eats the space.
const where = `${meet.venue}, ${meet.street}, ${meet.postcode}.`;

const perRun = formatPriceWords(prices.payPerRunPence);
const perYear = formatPriceWords(prices.membershipPerYearPence);

// The pace bands, plus the two groups that are not bands. The table itself is on
// `/run-with-us/#pace`; these are the shortest possible answer to "is there a group for me?"
const paceLabels = [
  'Walk-to-run',
  'Social, about 4 miles with rests',
  ...[...rows].reverse().map((row) => row.group.replace(':00', '')),
];
---

<ClubBase
  title="Southville Running Club — a friendly running club in South Bristol"
  description="A friendly running club of mixed abilities and ages 18+, meeting Tuesdays and Thursdays at the Southbank Club in Bedminster, Bristol. New runners always welcome."
  canonical="https://new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk/"
>
  <section class="club-hero">
    <div class="club-wrap club-hero-inner">
      <div>
        <h1>Come and run with us</h1>
        <p class="club-lede">
          A friendly club of mixed abilities and ages 18+. Whatever your pace, there's a
          group for you.
        </p>
        <p class="club-btns">
          <a class="club-btn club-btn-primary" href={CLUB_CTA.href}>{CLUB_CTA.label}</a>
          <a class="club-btn club-btn-secondary" href="/membership/">Join the club</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      {
        /* The alt text describes what is in the frame and claims nothing outside it — no
          place name, no date, no names. A reader who cannot see it should learn what the
          club looks like on an ordinary evening, which is the whole job of this picture. */
      }
      <Image
        class="club-hero-photo"
        src={heroPhoto}
        alt="Around eighteen Southville Running Club members, several in club green, gathered on a path through a cemetery at dusk before an evening run."
        widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1600]}
        sizes="(min-width: 62em) 46rem, 0px"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* ⚠️ **Inside the first screen on a 390×844 phone**, which is what the hidden hero photo
      pays for. Somebody who has just heard about the club wants the when and the where. */
  }
  <section class="club-facts" aria-labelledby="facts-heading">
    <div class="club-wrap">
      <h2 id="facts-heading" class="club-visually-hidden">When and where we run</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>When</b>{meet.days}</li>
        <li><b>Time</b>{meet.time}</li>
        <li>
          {
            /* ⚠️ **`{' '}` and not a literal space.** This is the third time this trap has
              been paid for on this branch: Prettier reflows `{where}` and the link onto
              separate lines, and Astro compresses the newline between them to **nothing** —
              so the strip rendered "BS3 1DB.Map". A space written as an expression is a
              token, and no formatter moves it. Composing in the frontmatter fixes the other
              two instances; it cannot fix this one, because half the join is a link. */
          }
          <b>Where</b>{where}{' '}<a href={meet.mapUrl}>Map</a>
        </li>
        <li><b>Cost</b>{perRun} a run</li>
        <li><b>Who</b>{who}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="club-sec">
    <div class="club-wrap">
      <h2>Your first run, in three steps</h2>
      <ol class="club-g3 club-steps">
        <li>
          <span class="club-step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <h3>Turn up on a Tuesday</h3>
          <p>
            Arrive by 6.10pm at the {meet.venue}. Tuesday is our busiest night, with 80 to
            100 runners and the most groups, including walk-to-run.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="club-step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <h3>Pick a pace group</h3>
          <p>
            Each group leader says what they're planning. Not sure? Ask one, and start in
            a slower group than you think.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="club-step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <h3>Run, then chat</h3>
          <p>
            Pop {perRun} in the pot. Most groups are back within the hour, and plenty of us
            stay for a drink at the {meet.venue}.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <a class="club-btn club-btn-primary" href="/run-with-us/"
          >Read the new runners' guide</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="club-sec club-sec-alt">
    <div class="club-wrap club-g2 club-split">
      <div>
        <h2>Tuesday or Thursday?</h2>
        <dl class="club-compare">
          <div>
            <dt>Tuesday</dt>
            <dd>
              80 to 100 runners, the widest choice of groups and the walk-to-run
              beginners' group. Best for your first time.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Thursday</dt>
            <dd>Around 30 runners. A smaller, quieter night.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>A group for every pace</h2>
        <ul class="club-pills">
          {paceLabels.map((label) => <li>{label}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <p>{alsoRunning}</p>
        <p><a href="/run-with-us/#pace">See the full pace guide</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="club-sec">
    <div class="club-wrap">
      <h2>Coming up</h2>
      <div class="club-g3">
        {
          upcoming.map((entry) => {
            const when = dateFor(entry.dateFrom);

            return (
              <article class="club-card">
                {/* Absent rather than empty when there is no date to show. */}
                {when !== null && <p class="club-small">{when}</p>}
                <h3>{entry.title}</h3>
                <p>{entry.summary}</p>
                <a class="club-btn club-btn-secondary" href={entry.href}>
                  {entry.cta}
                </a>
              </article>
            );
          })
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="club-sec club-sec-alt">
    <div class="club-wrap club-g2 club-split">
      <div>
        <h2>Join the club for {perYear} a year</h2>
        <p>
          You don't need to be a member to run with us. Membership supports the club and
          gets you into the members' WhatsApp community and local discounts. Racing a lot?
          Add an England Athletics licence.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="club-btn club-btn-primary" href="/membership/">
            Compare membership options
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>

      {
        /* ⚠️ **The whole club, next to the invitation to join it** — which is the one place
          on the site where showing *everyone* is the argument rather than a crowd shot. It
          also puts the wordmark burnt into this photograph a long way from the header's own,
          where it reads as a club banner rather than as the logo dropped in twice. */
      }
      <Image
        class="club-photo club-photo-wide"
        src={joinPhoto}
        alt="Around eighty Southville Running Club members in green club vests and race numbers, gathered on grass for a group photograph at a summer race."
        widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1640]}
        sizes="(min-width: 62em) 34rem, (min-width: 44em) 44vw, 90vw"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* ⚠️ **"What members say" is deliberately absent.** The mockup has three quotes, each
      attributed to "[Member name]" and tagged as a placeholder. A testimonial is a real person
      saying a real thing with their consent; until the club supplies one, the honest page is
      the one without the section. It is not greyed out, not stubbed, and not filled with a
      plausible quote — it simply is not here yet. */
  }
</ClubBase>
